{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogSincNearZero","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.LogSincNearZero","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevEndpointSplit","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TrapezoidRule","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SinCubeBounds","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CompositeEulerMaclaurin"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_sum_logSinc_sub_euler_maclaurin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_sum_logSinc_sub_euler_maclaurin","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L361-L428","doc":"**The Euler–Maclaurin expansion of `∑_{j=1}^{m+1} logSinc(jh)`.**\n\n    | ∑_{j=0}^{m} logSinc(h+jh)\n        − [ (1/h)∫_h^{h+mh} logSinc + ½(logSinc h + logSinc(h+mh))\n            + (h/12)(logSinc′(h+mh) − logSinc′(h)) ] |\n      ≤ (h²/12)·(logSinc″(h) − logSinc″(h+mh))\n\ni.e. the `B₂` term appears once and the error is `O(h²)` — an order below the\n`O(1/N)` term `qou-mlgp` (A) extracts.\n\nThis is `QOU.MathlibExt.abs_integral_sub_composite_le_osc` at `g = logSinc`,\n`a = h`, divided through by `h`.  The four hypotheses it needs are\n`hasDerivAt_logSinc`, `hasDerivAt_logSinc_deriv`, continuity of `logSinc″` (from\n`hasDerivAt_logSinc_deriv2`), and `antitoneOn_logSinc_deriv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.antitoneOn_logSinc_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.antitoneOn_logSinc_deriv","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L317-L352","doc":"**`logSinc″` is antitone on any `[c,d] ⊆ (0, π)`.**\n\n`logSinc‴ ≤ 0` there, because `2cos x/sin³x ≤ 2/x³` is exactly\n`x³·cos x ≤ sin³x` — `QOU.MathlibExt.mul_cube_cos_lt_sin_cube`.\n\nThis is the final hypothesis of\n`QOU.MathlibExt.abs_integral_sub_composite_le_osc`; with it, every input that\ncomposite rule asks for is available for `logSinc` on `[h, θ]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_logSinc_deriv2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_logSinc_deriv2","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L290-L315","doc":"`logSinc‴ x = −2/x³ + 2·cos x/sin³x` on `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_logSinc_deriv2_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_logSinc_deriv2_le","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L257-L286","doc":"**`|logSinc″ x| ≤ 1` on `(0,1]`.**\n\n`logSinc″ x = (sin²x − x²)/(x²sin²x)`, and `sin x < x`, `sin x > x − x³/4` give\n`x² − sin²x ≤ x⁴/2` and `x²sin²x ≥ 9x⁴/16`, so the quotient is at most `8/9`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_logSinc_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_logSinc_deriv","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L245-L255","doc":"`logSinc″ x = 1/x² − 1/sin²x` on `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_logSinc_deriv_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_logSinc_deriv_le","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L202-L219","doc":"**`|logSinc′ x| ≤ x` on `(0,1]`.**\n\n`logSinc′ x = cos x/sin x − 1/x = (x cos x − sin x)/(x sin x)`, and the two\nmonotonicity bounds above pin the numerator between `−x² sin x` and `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_logSinc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_logSinc","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L191-L200","doc":"`logSinc′ x = cos x/sin x − 1/x` on `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_sub_mul_cos_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_sub_mul_cos_lt","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L153-L189","doc":"`sin x − x·cos x < x²·sin x` on `(0,1]`.  From `v(0) = 0` and\n`v′ = x(sin x + x cos x) > 0`, using `cos > 0` on `(0,1] ⊆ (0, π/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_sub_mul_cos_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_sub_mul_cos_pos","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L128-L151","doc":"`sin x − x·cos x > 0` on `(0,1]`.  From `u(0) = 0` and `u′ = x·sin x > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_logSinc_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_logSinc_le","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L117-L124","doc":"The two-sided statement, packaged: `logSinc` is `O(x²)` near `0`, which is\nall `qou-mlgp` (A) needs from the left endpoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.neg_sq_div_three_le_logSinc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.neg_sq_div_three_le_logSinc","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L74-L115","doc":"**`−x²/3 ≤ logSinc x` on `(0, 1]`.**\n\n`sin x > x − x³/4` gives `sin x / x > 1 − x²/4 ≥ 3/4`, and\n`log t ≥ 1 − 1/t = (t−1)/t` (the `log y ≤ y − 1` bound at `y = 1/t`) turns that\ninto `logSinc x ≥ −(x²/4)/(3/4) = −x²/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.logSinc_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.logSinc_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSincNearZero.lean#L66-L72","doc":"`logSinc x ≤ 0` on `(0, π)` — immediate from `sin x < x`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}